    "evidence_text": "Robin Barton\n\nFunny Bones\n\n The music score was by John Altman, and the cinematography by Eduardo Serra.\n\nIvan Dragomiloff\n\n The character was played by actor Oliver Reed in the film of the same name.\n\nOliver Reed\n\n Notable films include \"The Trap\" (1966), \"Oliver!\n\nHarry Flashman\n\n Flashman was played by Malcolm McDowell in the Richard Lester 1975 film \"Royal Flash\".\n\nRoyal Flash (film)\nRoyal Flash is a 1975 film based on George MacDonald Fraser's second Flashman novel, \"Royal Flash\".\n It stars Malcolm McDowell as Flashman.\n Additionally, Oliver Reed appeared in the role of Otto von Bismarck, Alan Bates as Rudi von Sternberg, and Florinda Bolkan played Lola Montez.\n Fraser wrote the screenplay and the film was directed by Richard Lester.\n\nRoyal Flash\nRoyal Flash is a 1970 novel by George MacDonald Fraser.\n It is the second of the Flashman novels.\n It was made into the film \"Royal Flash\" in 1975 and remains the only Flashman novel to be filmed.\n\nThe Duke of Hamilton\n\n It was a popular meeting place for actors Peter O'Toole, Oliver Reed and Richard Burton.\n\n Reed would be seen for long periods at the pub on a daily basis.\n\nLion of the Desert\n\n .\n\nOtto von Bismarck\n\n This helped set the stage for the First World War.",
